{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"390","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Inna and Large Sweet Matrix"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Inna loves sweets very much. That's why she wants to play the \"Sweet Matrix\" game with Dima and Sereja. But Sereja is a large person, so the game proved small for him. Sereja suggested playing the \"Large Sweet Matrix\" game."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The \"Large Sweet Matrix\" playing field is an "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n × m"},{"kind":"text","text":" matrix. Let's number the rows of the matrix from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the columns — from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":". Let's denote the cell in the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th row and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th column as "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(i, j)"},{"kind":"text","text":". Each cell of the matrix can contain multiple candies, initially all cells are empty. The game goes in "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"w"},{"kind":"text","text":" moves, during each move one of the two following events occurs:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Sereja chooses five integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x1, y1, x2, y2, v"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x1 ≤ x2, y1 ≤ y2)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and adds "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":" candies to each matrix cell "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(i, j)"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x1 ≤ i ≤ x2; y1 ≤ j ≤ y2)"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Sereja chooses four integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x1, y1, x2, y2"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x1 ≤ x2, y1 ≤ y2)"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then he asks Dima to calculate the total number of candies in cells "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(i, j)"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x1 ≤ i ≤ x2; y1 ≤ j ≤ y2)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and he asks Inna to calculate the total number of candies in the cells of matrix "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(p, q)"},{"kind":"text","text":", which meet the following logical criteria: ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"p < x1"},{"kind":"text","text":" OR "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"p > x2"},{"kind":"text","text":") AND ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"q < y1"},{"kind":"text","text":" OR "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"q > y2"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Finally, Sereja asks to write down the difference between the number Dima has calculated and the number Inna has calculated (D - I). "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Unfortunately, Sereja's matrix is really huge. That's why Inna and Dima aren't coping with the calculating. Help them!"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains three integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"w"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(3 ≤ n, m ≤ 4·106; 1 ≤ w ≤ 105)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"w"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines describe the moves that were made in the game. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" A line that describes an event of the first type contains 6 integers: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x1"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y1"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x2"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y2"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ x1 ≤ x2 ≤ n; 1 ≤ y1 ≤ y2 ≤ m; 1 ≤ v ≤ 109)"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" A line that describes an event of the second type contains 5 integers: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x1"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y1"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x2"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y2"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(2 ≤ x1 ≤ x2 ≤ n - 1; 2 ≤ y1 ≤ y2 ≤ m - 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the second type move occurs at least once. It is guaranteed that a single operation will not add more than "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"109"},{"kind":"text","text":" candies."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Be careful, the constraints are very large, so please use optimal data structures. Max-tests will be in pretests."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each second type move print a single integer on a single line — the difference between Dima and Inna's numbers."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4 5 5\n0 1 1 2 3 2\n0 2 2 3 3 3\n0 1 5 4 5 1\n1 2 3 3 4\n1 3 4 3 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n-21\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note to the sample. After the first query the matrix looks as: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n22200\n22200 \n00000\n00000\n"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After the second one it is: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n22200\n25500\n03300 \n00000\n"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After the third one it is: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n22201\n25501\n03301\n00001\n"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the fourth query, Dima's sum equals 5 + 0 + 3 + 0 = 8 and Inna's sum equals 4 + 1 + 0 + 1 = 6. The answer to the query equals 8 - 6 = 2. For the fifth query, Dima's sum equals 0 and Inna's sum equals 18 + 2 + 0 + 1 = 21. The answer to the query is 0 - 21 = -21."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"390E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/390/problem/E"}